# PowerPC Darwin OS personality for hyper-linux.app — .plan

Status: proposed / not executed. The 20 `.goal` cards are executable work items.

## Scope
PowerPC Mac OS X 10.4/10.5 32-bit guest applications through `hl`, with wine-style guest libraries and native user-provided historical system bundle modes. CLI and guest OS compatibility here; UI implementation tracked separately in `ppc-darwin-ui`.

## Architectural placement
Existing `ppc32rt` stays tiny; `hl` owns guest Mach-O, dyld, Mach/BSD personality, framework resolution and application lifecycle. Reuse iOS implementation after code inspection; never assume ABI identity.

## Established inputs (user-reported; not independently verified)
- `hyper-linux.app` (`hl`) already has Android APK graphics/input/audio (`hl Minecraft.apk`), iOS UI work, X11 (`hl XMMS` partially works), and iOS guest Mach-O/Mach facilities in wine-style and native-bundle modes.
- Treat these as existing capabilities to inspect and reuse, not as verified guarantees for PowerPC Darwin.

## Two compatibility modes
- **Wine-style**: `hl` supplies guest ABI-compatible compatibility libraries, shims and stubs; explicit errors for unsupported APIs.
- **Native**: user-supplied historical PPC Darwin system/framework bundle, dyld and frameworks executed as guest code where feasible; `hl` supplies kernel, service and presentation contracts.
- Mixed resolution must be deterministic, auditable and avoid host/guest ABI confusion.

## Ownership
- `ppc32rt`: minimal guest execution engine, CPU/exception state, guest-memory operations and narrow trap callback ABI; no Mach-O framework policy, windowing or audio.
- `hyper-linux.app`: app discovery, Mach-O loading, dyld/framework resolution, Mach/BSD personality, lifecycle, service bridge, graphics, input, audio, X11, testing and packaging.
- Cross-repo interface must be versioned and independently testable; copy-first rt-series invariants remain intact.

