## Parallel lanes
Lane A: ppc32rt CPU/trap; Lane B: hl Mach-O/dyld; Lane C: hl Mach/BSD/threads; Lane D: bundle and native libraries; Lane E: qualification and security.

## Integration gates
- Gate A: inventory current `hl`/iOS/Android/X11 functionality and preserve known-good behavior.
- Gate B: minimal PowerPC Darwin static CLI under interpreter; malformed binaries rejected safely.
- Gate C: wine-style dynamic CLI and native-bundle dynamic CLI independently verified.
- Gate D: interpreter/DBT parity and Mach/BSD/thread/fault correctness under repeatable tests.
- Gate E: UI tests include real windows, input, audio and lifecycle; X11, Carbon and Cocoa reported separately, not conflated.
- Gate F: security, regressions, cold/warm AOT, licensing/provenance and release matrix reviewed.

## Risk register
Historical Darwin PPC trap and framework ABIs differ from iOS; guest kernel and service expectations remain difficult. System bundle licensing and provenance must be respected.

## Qualification and reporting
Use `rt-series` broad then subsystem-specific convergence audits; verify on actual supported host environments, record fixture hashes and commands, compare interpreter/DBT and external reference where available. Do not claim QEMU Linux user-mode is a Darwin OS oracle.

## Out of scope
Classic Mac OS 9, arbitrary macOS versions, unlicensed redistribution, guaranteed complete Carbon/Cocoa compatibility, and ppc64 Darwin without a separate feasibility gate.

## Completion
All 20 cards closed with reproducible evidence and no untriaged high-severity defects for the declared release profile.
